NAME
    ls - list a directory

SYNOPSIS
    ls [-l] [DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    List the entries of DIR, or of the working directory when none is
    given. Directories are shown with a trailing '/'.

    DIR may be absolute or relative to the working directory. A path that
    names a regular file is refused with "not a directory", and one that
    names nothing with "no such directory": the two are different facts and
    are reported as such.

OPTIONS
    -l      long format: the mode (drwxr-xr-x), the owner and the size of
            each entry.

SECURITY
    The listing is read through the fs_server, which shows only what your
    login may see. When you hold a directory capability, entries the
    filesystem policy withholds from you are absent, not refused (see
    fs.policy(5)).

EXIT STATUS
    ls is a shell builtin and sets no exit status.

SEE ALSO
    cd(1), stat(1), mkdir(1), hier(7)
